@startuml timing_reactionTime
' ============================================================
' Timing: Reaction Time Model
' Shows clean-start and foul-start on a shared time axis.
' Times are illustrative (not real race values).
' ============================================================

title Timing: Reaction Time Model [DerbyTrack — Reaction Mode]

robust  "Race State\n(startController)"  as RS
robust  "Gate — clean lane"              as GC
concise "Button — clean lane"            as BC
robust  "Gate — foul lane"               as GF
concise "Button — foul lane"             as BF
robust  "Finish Sensor (both)"           as FS

' ============================================================
' COUNTDOWN phase (0 ms - 2000 ms)
' ============================================================
@0
RS is COUNTDOWN
GC is UP
BC is released
GF is UP
BF is released
FS is waiting

@500
note top of RS : Y3

@1000
note top of RS : Y2

@1500
note top of RS : Y1

' ============================================================
' Foul: button pressed BEFORE GO (during countdown)
' ============================================================
@1800
BF is pressed
note top of BF
  [FOUL] button pressed 200 ms
  before GO during countdown.
  carStartUs = 1800 ms
  gate drops immediately.
end note

@1800
GF is DOWN

' ============================================================
' GO: raceStartUs captured
' ============================================================
@2000
RS is RACING
note top of RS
  GO reached (CD_GO).
  raceStartUs = micros()
  = 2000 ms reference point.
end note

' ============================================================
' Clean: button pressed AFTER GO (during racing)
' ============================================================
@2200
BC is pressed
note top of BC
  [CLEAN] button pressed 200 ms
  after GO.
  carStartUs = 2200 ms
  gate drops now.
end note

@2200
GC is DOWN

' ============================================================
' Both sensors trigger (same finish time for comparison)
' ============================================================
@5000
FS is TRIGGERED
note bottom of FS
  raceTimeUs = 3000 ms
  (sensor elapsed since raceStartUs)
end note

@5200
RS is COMPLETE

' ============================================================
' Annotations: reaction time math
' ============================================================
note bottom of GC
  CLEAN START:
  reactionTimeUs = carStartUs - raceStartUs = 2200 - 2000 = 200 ms
  carTimeUs = raceTimeUs - reactionTimeUs  = 3000 - 200  = 2800 ms
  (reward: clean reaction subtracted from elapsed time)
end note

note bottom of GF
  FOUL START:
  reactionTimeUs = raceStartUs - carStartUs = 2000 - 1800 = 200 ms
  carTimeUs = raceTimeUs + reactionTimeUs  = 3000 + 200  = 3200 ms
  (penalty: foul reaction added to elapsed time)
end note

note bottom of FS
  calcReactionTimes(foul, raceStartUs, carStartUs):
  . foul=true:  return elapsed(raceStart, carStart)
                raceStart > carStart (early press)
  . foul=false: return elapsed(carStart, raceStart)
                carStart > raceStart (late press)
  Both return a positive uint32_t reaction time in microseconds.
end note

@enduml
